From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 08:17:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] yang: snooping models without references into
 sonic-vlan/port/portchannel

With #24327's two models installed, 7 sonic-utilities tests of the
generic config updater fail (gu_common_test TestPathAddressing,
patch_sorter_test), and the sonic-utilities wheel -- whose tests run in
the image build -- does not build. Bisected in the bookworm build slave:
any module that imports sonic-vlan (even one with a single leafref to a
VLAN name) changes the references GCU's libyang 1 walk reports for the
existing tables (VLAN_MEMBER starts showing up as a reference to PORT);
an unrelated module does not, and neither model without the imports
does. That is GCU's behaviour for config apply-patch/replace changing
under the image, not just a test.

So the interface and VLAN-name fields become plain strings and the
imports of sonic-vlan, sonic-port and sonic-portchannel go; the
structure, ranges, enums and must checks stay. All 214 tests of the two
GCU test files pass and all 141 models load. What is lost is YANG's
check that a named VLAN or port exists; the snooping CLI writes through
an unvalidated ConfigDBConnector and the disunified driver writes rows
directly, so nothing in this build depends on it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
